@startuml
' Source block: uml251_03_components_composite_structure (uml-2.5.1-legend.puml intake)
!include ../../../../tooling/styles/plantuml/structural/composite-structure-diagram-style.iuml
' ============================================================================
' Section 03 — Components and composite structure
'
' UML traceability:
'   UML 2.5.1 §11.2 Structured Classifiers
'   UML 2.5.1 §11.3 Encapsulated Classifiers / Ports
'   UML 2.5.1 §11.6 Components
'
' PlantUML support is Partial:
'   components, interfaces, and ports are native;
'   precise UML Part, assembly-Connector, delegation-Connector,
'   and provided/required Interface semantics are not fully encoded.
' ============================================================================

title UML 2.5.1 Notation Reference — Components and Composite Structure
left to right direction
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam componentStyle uml2

component "Order Service" as OrderService {
  port "api : IOrder" as orderApi
  port "payment : IPayment" as paymentPort

  component "worker : Worker" as WorkerPart {
    port "in" as workerIn
  }
}

() "IOrder" as IOrder
() "IPayment" as IPayment

IOrder -- orderApi : provided Interface\n(lollipop rendering)
paymentPort ..> IPayment : required Interface\nUsage mapping

orderApi -- workerIn : delegation Connector\n(approx.)

component "Producer" as Producer {
  portout "events" as producerEvents
}

component "Consumer" as Consumer {
  portin "events" as consumerEvents
}

producerEvents -- consumerEvents : assembly Connector\n(approx.)

interface "ServiceContract" as ServiceContract
component "ServiceImpl" as ServiceImpl
ServiceContract <|.. ServiceImpl : Component/Interface realization

note bottom of OrderService
  <b>UML semantics</b>
  Port = Property specifying a distinct interaction point.
  Provided Interfaces characterize requests the environment
  may make to the encapsulated classifier.
  Required Interfaces characterize requests the classifier
  expects its environment to support.

  PlantUML port / portin / portout are renderer constructs;
  do not infer UML provided/required semantics from their names alone.
end note

note bottom of WorkerPart
  UML parts are Properties in a StructuredClassifier.
  Nested PlantUML components are used here only as a visual
  approximation of a white-box internal structure.
end note

legend
  |= UML concept |= PlantUML support |
  | Component | Native |
  | Interface / lollipop | Native |
  | Port | Native renderer primitive |
  | Provided / required Interface semantics | Partial |
  | Part / Property in internal structure | Approximation |
  | Assembly Connector | Approximation |
  | Delegation Connector | Approximation |
  | ComponentRealization | Native relationship notation |
endlegend
@enduml
